# Lilah's "exile that spell instead ... If you do, it becomes plotted" set on Bot1's Lightning Helix, then Bot2 takes the
# Helix with Sudden Substitution (and the Memnite goes to Bot1) and retargets it at Bot1. As the Helix resolves Bot2 controls
# it, so Bot2 orders Lilah's exile and Rest in Peace (CR 616.1, the affected object's controller): Rest in Peace first, and
# the Helix is exiled unplotted - Bot1 can not cast it from exile on a later turn.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Lilah, Undefeated Slickshot
Rest in Peace
Lightning Helix
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Memnite
Sudden Substitution
Island
Island x23

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
